  "scope": "Unchanged core/game/ge (GrandExchange with its start-up listener, worker loop body, matching, dispatch, bot offers, queries and command definitions; GrandExchangeOffer; GrandExchangeRecords with the login/save/parse hooks, collection box, history log and init; GrandExchangeTimer.run; GEDB; PriceIndex/PriceInfo; GEGuidePrice; GEItemSet; OfferState; BotPrices; GEAutoStock), content/global/handlers/iface/ge (StockMarket, GrandExchangeInterface, ExchangeItemSets), InterfaceContainer, GrandExchangePacket, LoginListener, PersistPlayer, StartupListener, InterfaceListener/InterfaceListeners, IntType, ContentInterface, IfaceSettingsBuilder, InputType, RunScript.processInput, DialogueConst, IronmanManager/IronmanMode, Definition, Item, Container with ContainerEvent/ContainerListener/ContainerType/SortType, Component, ComponentDefinition, ComponentPlugin, CloseEvent, InterfaceType, Plugin, Initializable, the complete InterfaceManager, ClientInfo, IoBuffer and the WindowsPane, Interface, CloseInterface, InterfaceConfig, Config, RunScriptPacket, StringPacket, AccessMask and ContainerPacket writers with their contexts, on JDK 11 with sqlite-jdbc 3.36.0.3, each case in a fresh class loader over its own database file, with the pinned interface_configs.json. Original text inserted at generation time: SQLiteProvider (initTables, run, connect, TABLE_CHECK; the coroutine members runAsync/pruneOldData are left out and the connection is wrapped by a proxy that records each executeQuery/executeUpdate/execute with its bound parameters); PacketProcessor.process's GESetOfferItem branch; ContentAPI getAttribute, setAttribute, removeAttribute, openInterface, closeInterface, inInventory, amountInInventory, hasSpaceFor, itemDefinition, getItemName, both sendInputDialogue forms and hasAwaitingGrandExchangeCollections; PacketDispatch sendString, sendIfaceSettings, sendRunScript and sendInterfaceConfig; StringUtils.formatDisplayName; Location.transform; Node and the ItemDefinition members the classes reach; InterfaceConfigParser with a string reader. ContentAPI removeItem/addItem keep their INVENTORY branch. Recording adapters: Player (attributes as a map, uid, artificial flag and bank PIN state from the case), PlayerDetails (getDetails), the session (fixed mode, zero ISAAC), Player.sendMessage, PacketDispatch.sendMessage after its null return, ContentAPI sendMessage/notify/setVarp/playAudio/playJingle/log, SystemLogger.logGE, Repository (players, uid_map, sendGrandExchangeNews), Discord.postNewOffer, CS2Mapping.forId, ItemDefinition.getExamine, GameWorld.Pulser.submit, the Commands definitions (bodies run by the case), RSTimer's constructor, ServerConstants from the case, System.currentTimeMillis of core.game.ge (a case clock with a step per read) and an inventory listener that records update slots and refreshes. Modelled in Support.java: the tail of processIfAction (component lookup, hidden check, ButtonClickEvent, InterfaceListeners.run, plugin), the InputPromptResponse branch around RunScript.processInput, the worker thread (the body boot() starts runs on the case thread at each \"worker\" action until pendingOffers is empty: pendingOffers is replaced at class load by a deque whose takeFirst ends the step instead of blocking; an exception ends the thread for good), pulses run at each \"pulse\" action, and GEAutoStock's relative file under the JVM's working directory. Not exercised: concurrent execution of the worker and the world thread, the SQLiteProvider lock timeouts, Discord webhooks, the real InventoryListener, GameMessage bytes and the real item cache (definitions are authored inputs).",
